<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Differentiation by Power rule</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given that \( f(x)={@f(x)@}\)</p>
<p>Find:</p></p>
<ol class="HELM_parts">
<li>\(f({@p1@})=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] </li>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]] </p>
<li>\(f'(x)=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] </li>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]] </p>
<li>\(f'({@p2@})=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] </li>
<p>[[feedback:prt3]] </p>
<li>\(f''(x)=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] </li>
<p>[[feedback:prt4]] </p>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked  Solution</h3>
<p>Given that \( f(x)={@f(x)@}\)</p>
<ol class="HELM_parts">
  <li>
    <p>To find \(f({@p1@})\), we simply need to substitute \(x\) with {@p1@} in the function \(f(x)\):</p>
    <p>\(f({@x@}) = {@f(x)@}\)</p>
    <p>\( \displaystyle \begin{align*} 
              f({@p1@}) &= {@cf1@}({@p1@})^{@pwr1@} + {@cf2@}({@p1@})^2 + {@cf3@}({@p1@}) + {@cf4@} \\
                                &=  {@cf1*(p1^pwr1)@} + {@cf2*(p1^2)@} + {@cf3*p1@} + {@cf4@} \\
                                 &= {@ta1@} \end{align*} \)</p>
    <p>So, \(f({@p1@}) = {@ta1@}\).</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>To find \(f'(x)\), we'll need to take the derivative of the function \(f(x)\) with respect to \(x\), using Power rule</p>
     <p>The power rule is as follows:</p>
    <p>If \( \displaystyle f(x) = ax^n\), where \(a\) and \(n\) are constants, then the derivative \(f'(x)\) is given by:</p>
     <p>\( \displaystyle f'(x) = n \cdot ax^{n-1}\)</p>
  <p>\(f(x) = {@f(x)@}\)</p>
<p> \( \displaystyle \begin{align*}  f'(x) &= \frac{d}{dx}(f(x)) \\
                           &= \frac{d}{dx}({@f(x)@}) \\
                           &= {@ta2@} \end{align*} \)</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>To find \(f'({@p2@})\), substitute \(x\) with {@p2@} in the derivative \(f'(x)\):</p>
    <p>\(f'({@x@}) = {@ta2@}\) </p>
    <p>\(f'({@p2@}) = {@ta3@}\) </p>
<p>So, \(f'({@p2@}) = {@ta3@}\).</p>
  </li>
<li>
<p> The second derivative \(f''(x)\):</p>
<p> \( \displaystyle \begin{align*} f''(x) &= \frac{d}{dx}\left({@ta2@}\right) \\
                    &= {@ta4@} \end{align*} \)</p>
</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
